{"game": "deep-rock-galactic", "language": "english", "appid": 548430, "month": "2019-08", "window": 4, "start_date": 1566604800, "end_date": 1567295999, "month_true_total": 122, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-08-29 21:20:06 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "54908717", "author": {"steamid": "76561198116981436", "personaname": "Blackwater", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198116981436/", "num_games_owned": 108, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 6042, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2081, "last_played": 1732772450, "avatar": "4b8e97e671dd7208a80bd29dd2786a4dda5da9a8"}, "language": "english", "review": "While many gameplay elements may be familiar to players starting off Deep Rock Galactic, from the co-op shooter aspect aesthetically reminding one of the two left 4 dead iterations to the geometric procedurally generated levels, the game is a far fetch from either.\n\nWhat we have instead is a fantastic co-op shooter with ever deepening levels of difficulty, making for a smooth transition from a simple mining mission into a hellscape, where suddenly the somber blue collar gallows humor makes infinitely more sense; and the question of \"what happened to Karl?\" less of a mystery than a reality. \n\nThe cooperative element is only furthered by the support tools available to each class. While you wont be punished for going off on your own directly, you will be met with the challenge of getting any worth out of a mission by going it alone. The core element of fulfilling a quota demands cooperation for expedience, or a gruesome death at the hands of the horde with no ammo left to fight.\n\nLeave no dwarf behind.", "timestamp_created": 1567287274, "timestamp_updated": 1567287274, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.519057750701904297", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": fa